Problem: (r5) the dark theme used dark-grey surfaces (#1d1b1f / #312f33 / #42414d etc.), not true black, so AMOLED pixels stay lit. (r6) after the r5 remap, the Settings page became a pure-black void: androidx.preference rows are transparent ripples on the fragment backdrop and its list dividers are #1f000000, so the whole page read as an empty black screen; the r6 fix added #1A1A1A card rows, which the user rejected as a "mix of gray and pureblack". (r7) this revision removes every gray fill: all surface/container/layer tokens are now pure black, and structure is carried by 1dp hairlines instead of lit-gray fills.
Root cause: values-night/colors.xml maps the Material3 surface tokens to novaGray65-85 (dark greys) and layer tokens to photonDarkGrey30/80 — none are #000000, so AMOLED pixels stay on (r5). The r6 settings void is caused by the preference stack itself: androidx.preference 1.2.1 paints no row background, and its divider drawable is #1f000000 — all structure carriers vanished once the backdrop became #000000. The r7 remaining gray is the r6 container scale itself (#0A0A0A-#242424) plus outline/layer tokens that still referenced dark greys.
Affected layer: app UI resources only (values-night/colors.xml, values/styles.xml, drawable/, layout/). No Kotlin, no GeckoView, no build config.
Implementation: keep the true-black AMOLED base and collapse the entire elevation scale to #000000: background/surface/dim/surface_variant/surface_bright, all surface_container_* tokens, layer_color_2 (cards/menus/dialogs), layer_color_3 (search), and the splashscreen background (#210340 purple -> pure black for an instant-black AMOLED splash). Structure now comes from hairlines: outline #2A2A2A / outline_variant #242424, and the settings row card (op7_preference_row_background) gets a 1dp #242424 stroke around its pure-black fill via PreferenceTheme.preferenceStyle + SwitchCompatPreferenceMaterialStyle; androidx list dividers stay neutralized. Row layout is a pinned copy of androidx.preference 1.2.1 preference_material.
Expected benefit: maximum AMOLED power saving — every non-content pixel on UI chrome (toolbar, menus, dialogs, home, settings, splash) is now truly off, with card structure preserved by hairlines that cost ~0 pixels. Measurable via screen-on drain deltas and black-pixel coverage screenshots (before/after).
Benchmark: r5 baseline in docs/performance/ (black-pixel coverage + screen-on mA method). r7 target: 100% pure-black coverage on UI chrome surfaces (vs r5 ~10% pure black), settings rows visible via hairline (visual QA), no regression in on-surface text contrast. No frame-time claim.
Regression risk: cosmetic/theme only; on-surface text stays near-white (#f2f0f8) on pure black. Home cards now blend into the backdrop (structure carried by content, not fills) — intentional pure-black look. Row layout is a pinned copy of androidx.preference 1.2.1 — an upstream bump that changes that layout surfaces as a patch conflict and stops the pipeline (by design). Light theme untouched. Revert = drop patch.
Upstream relationship: not for upstream (device-specific AMOLED preference + settings visibility); Fenix deliberately uses Material dark greys and flat preference rows. Could be proposed as an optional AMOLED toggle later.

diff --git a/app/src/main/res/drawable-v21/preference_list_divider_material.xml b/app/src/main/res/drawable-v21/preference_list_divider_material.xml
